<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "When should a Dubai salon start promoting Ramadan and Eid offers?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Work backwards from your own booking data: Eid appointments tend to fill early, so announce availability and open the diary several weeks ahead rather than in the final days. Check last year's booking dates to see how early your clients actually book."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does a salon need a different marketing plan for summer in Dubai?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Usually yes. Many residents travel in summer, so demand patterns shift. Look at your own appointment history, then lean on membership or package reminders, quieter-day offers and pre-travel and return-from-travel services instead of acquisition spend."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How far ahead should a salon plan its marketing calendar?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Plan the full year in outline and the next quarter in detail. A one-page calendar with the main demand moments, a start date for each and a named owner is enough for most salons."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Should a salon discount during slow seasons?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Not automatically. Discounts train clients to wait. Try added-value options first, such as a priority slot, a complimentary add-on that costs you little, or a package that fills quiet weekdays, and check the margin before launch."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What should a salon do after a busy peak like Eid?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Follow up with the new clients who came in, invite them to rebook at checkout or by message, and review which slots and services sold out. The weeks after a peak are when a first visit either becomes a regular or is forgotten."}}]}</script>

			
			
